Why This Is Asked
- Tests a practical, scalable multi-tenant pattern within a single bucket, emphasizing isolation, encryption, and rapid containment.
- Exercises policy design using S3, KMS, and IAM with MFA, plus a real-time breach response workflow.

Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation via per-tenant S3 prefix and IAM role scope
- SSE-KMS with per-tenant CMKs and encryption context validation
- Containment orchestration using EventBridge, Lambda, and CloudTrail

Code Example
```json
// S3 bucket policy (illustrative)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/Tenant123Role"},
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket/tenant-123/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"s3:prefix": "tenant-123/"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// KMS key policy (illustrative)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/Tenant123Role"},
      "Action": ["kms:Encrypt","kms:Decrypt"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"kms:EncryptionContext:TenantID": "tenant-123"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the 60-second containment workflow end-to-end? 
- How would you extend this to support new tenants without increasing policy complexity?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of secure software supply chain, artifact provenance, and rapid containment in a multi-account AWS setup.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Signer and CodePipeline integration for artifact signing and deployment
- Secrets Manager rotation, IAM role containment, EventBridge-triggered remediation
- Tenant isolation via per-tenant resources; rollback with immutable manifests using S3 Object Lock
- Tamper detection and audit trails via CloudTrail, Config, GuardDuty

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: Lambda handler triggered on tamper alert
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const tenant = event.detail.tenant;
  await revokeRoles(tenant);
  await rotateSecrets(tenant);
  quarantineTenantVPC(tenant);
  rollbackManifest(tenant);
  logAudit(tenant, event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the containment workflow to meet 60-second SLO?
- What failure modes require manual escalation and how to handle them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement tenant isolation with least privilege, plus rapid containment using AWS-native controls. It also covers S3 prefix scoping, per-tenant KMS keys, CloudTrail data events, and automated revocation.

## Key Concepts
- Least privilege IAM for Lambda and prefix-scoped S3 access
- S3 bucket policies with bucket-level and object-prefix constraints
- Per-tenant KMS keys and rotation
- CloudTrail Data Events for S3 access
- EventBridge-based containment workflow (60s)

## Code Example
```javascript
// IAM policy snippet for Lambda role
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake",
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/tenant-id-${aws:PrincipalTag tenantId}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringLike": {"s3:prefix": "tenant-id-*"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle role cred leakage or bucket misconfiguration?
- How would you test the containment workflow end-to-end?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time detection and automated containment of credential abuse in a multi-account CI/CD setup using OIDC tokens.

## Key Concepts
- OIDC-based cross-account access and trust policies
- Real-time threat detection: CloudTrail, Security Hub, IAM Access Analyzer
- Containment automation: credential rotation, trust policy adjustments, resource quarantine
- Automation tooling: EventBridge, Step Functions, Secrets Manager

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: IAM trust policy snippet with OIDC
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"Federated": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub": "repo:org/repo:ref:refs/heads/main"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the containment playbook?
- Which logs and metrics confirm rollback reliability and minimal pipeline disruption?
